@@ -0,0 +1,1094 @@
+# Animation names, one per line, numbered by position starting at @first (the AnimationData row id).
+#
+# Sources:
+#   * ids 466-1491: Marlamin's AnimationData name list (gist 91e5f37a1ba4d2276550525133095f5b, June 2020),
+#     numbered by position. Checked against: ids 466-505 (this client's own enum, every name reproduced exactly),
+#     ids 469 and 471 (the wowdev M2/AnimationList snippet: FlyDeathStart / FlyDeathEnd), and ids 548-574 (the
+#     modern-M2 extension's remap table: MountFlightIdle / Left / Right / Run / WalkBackwards, MountFlightStart /
+#     Land / LandRun).
+#   * ids 1731-1777: wowdev M2/AnimationList, explicit ids (Dragonflight sections, up to 10.2.6.53840).
+#   * ids 1492-1730: NO NAMES AVAILABLE when this was written. They are generated as ANIM_UNNAMED_<id>
+#     placeholders so the table is dense up to 1777 and ANIM_COUNT is correct. Replace the '@unnamed' line with the
+#     real names (start with an explicit id: "1492 SomeName", then one name per line) and re-run the generator;
+#     nothing in the client refers to the placeholders by name.
+#   * The list ends at 1777 (FlyMountMedium): animations added after 10.2.6 are not included.
+#
+# To add newer animations: append names (they take the next id), or start a line with an explicit id
+# ("1492 SomeNewName") to resume after a gap, then run gen_anim_enum.py.
+#
+# Ids 466-505 overlap the enum that already existed; the generator verifies them and only emits ids from 506.
